    {
      "id": "CAV-02",
      "title": "Why the central average preserves periods and the height exponent",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-central-cycle",
      "statement": "For each finite bar cycle the period of one central pullback equals the original period by the basepoint prism. Integrating over the unit interval and iterating preserves all periods, the simplex cocycle equation, arithmetic invariance and the original height exponent.",
